{"version":"1","id":"honeypot","handle":"honeypot","name":"Honeypot","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/1cc3a75b98b74698a40f57162b30b841","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-5.3666,"y":1.8456,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":385,"newest_post_at":"2026-04-30T15:00:18.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2020-10-13T12:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.007792,"listicle_ratio":0.145455,"question_ratio":0.062338,"avg_read_time":5.492447,"summary_length_avg":341.410557,"title_length_avg":50.807792,"title_length_var":290.394225,"tag_entropy":4.214281,"tag_diversity":0.423377,"top_tag_share":0.096104,"avg_upvotes":18.215584,"median_upvotes":3.0,"avg_comments":1.412987,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.077702,"zero_engagement_share":0.298701,"viral_share":0.044156,"posts_per_week":1.339371,"non_article_ratio":0.431169,"author_present_share":0.002597,"recency_skew":0.054795},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.5147,7.1324],"cadence_depth":[7.6471,-1.0],"hype_variety":[0.2941,8.4265],"title_style":[6.8382,9.6912]},"top_tags":[["general-programming",70],["webdev",56],["open-source",51],["python",40],["react",40],["javascript",35],["career",33],["angular",25]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["How to Build a Personal Brand as a Developer","8 Best Cheatsheets For React Developers","Git Commands - Cheat Sheet for All Developers"],"outlier":["47% of Developers Say Bad Project Managers Are Their Biggest Problem - and Other Learnings from our Developer Ambitions REPORT"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"qe7by0FJx","title":"The Zen of Python (import this)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BFOOO2BG8pY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-zen-of-python-import-this--qe7by0fjx","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/BFOOO2BG8pY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-30T15:00:18.000Z"},{"id":"cNAjZtsuK","title":"The creator of Apache Storm spent 10 years building this new programming paradigm","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hwi2NskMC-I","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-creator-of-apache-storm-spent-10-years-building-this-new-programming-paradigm-cnajztsuk","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/hwi2NskMC-I/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29T17:30:12.000Z"},{"id":"ZXXyFBjZ2","title":"Paul Graham, Lisp, and Clojure","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2ygsCkyzmcc","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/paul-graham-lisp-and-clojure-zxxyfbjz2","summary":"Developers share how Paul Graham's essays and books on Lisp \u2014 particularly 'Beating the Averages' and 'On Lisp' \u2014 inspired them to seek out a Lisp-based language. Common Lisp fell short due to library gaps and deployment friction, but Clojure's JVM targeting solved the practical adoption problem, making it an attractive entry point into the Lisp world.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2ygsCkyzmcc/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-23T16:45:00.000Z"},{"id":"4OEhohNL4","title":"Moving to Lisp from C++ felt like freedom","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-UGCtR0Ong0","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/moving-to-lisp-from-c-felt-like-freedom-4oehohnl4","summary":"A developer shares their experience switching from C++ to Common Lisp, describing it as liberating. They found Common Lisp simpler and more expressive than C++, allowing them to focus on actual problems like yield management systems and music software schedulers rather than fighting the language's type system and templates.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/-UGCtR0Ong0/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-21T18:30:01.000Z"},{"id":"fhoQzSVoy","title":"Why one of the world's largest digital banks chose Clojure","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pleo1VA9D70","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/why-one-of-the-world-s-largest-digital-banks-chose-clojure-fhoqzsvoy","summary":"Nubank co-founder Edward Wible and distinguished engineer Lucas Cavalcanti explain why the fintech giant chose Clojure as its primary backend language. Inspired by the 'Out of the Tar Pit' paper, the founding team concluded that mutable state and side effects are the root of accidental complexity in large systems. This led them to Clojure's functional programming model and Datomic's immutable database, which offered time-travel queries and full audit history \u2014 a natural fit for banking's regulatory requirements. Clojure's JVM foundation also gave access to the mature Java library ecosystem, letting the team focus on business problems rather than rebuilding infrastructure.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/pleo1VA9D70/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-19T18:00:51.000Z"},{"id":"jw13zxJrj","title":"How JetBrains survived competing against free Eclipse with a paid IntelliJ IDEA","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bS4MJtTu1JQ","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/intellij-idea-vs-eclipse-how-jetbrains-survived-the-odds-jw13zxjrj","summary":"JetBrains co-founders recount how IntelliJ IDEA survived fierce competition against Eclipse, a free IDE backed by IBM and other large companies. Despite being a paid product facing pressure from former employers, Microsoft recruitment attempts, and a well-funded competitor rapidly copying their features, JetBrains persisted by focusing on quality and listening to loyal users. Eclipse was dominant because it was free, but IntelliJ attracted developers willing to pay for a superior tool, allowing JetBrains to slowly grow and ultimately outlast the competition.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bS4MJtTu1JQ/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-20T14:01:03.000Z"},{"id":"isTNqS12S","title":"Java: The Documentary is Coming Soon","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cwLYS_xDvSw","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/java-the-documentary-is-coming-soon-istnqs12s","summary":"A documentary about the history of Java programming language is coming soon. The teaser features quotes from key figures reflecting on Java's origins, its rise to ubiquity, near-death moments, and eventual world domination as a mainstream platform. The narrative frames Java's journey as a dramatic multi-act story of faith, skepticism, and ultimate triumph.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/cwLYS_xDvSw/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-17T17:01:04.000Z"},{"id":"2ECXVSJWn","title":"Cult.Repo 2026 content preview teaser","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=royY-_f2byY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/coming-to-cult-repo-in-2026--2ecxvsjwn","summary":"A teaser or preview post for upcoming content on Cult.Repo in 2026, featuring dramatic quotes hinting at high-stakes tech entrepreneurship and experimentation. The content is a promotional snippet with no technical substance.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/royY-_f2byY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-16T01:24:29.000Z"},{"id":"mfQsSDzed","title":"IntelliJ's early struggle & Microsoft's persistent pressure","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K8opvOlnnQQ","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/intellij-s-early-struggle-microsoft-s-persistent-pressure-mfqssdzed","summary":"A founder of JetBrains reflects on the early days of IntelliJ IDEA, describing the challenges of being a minority player in the IDE market and the persistent pressure from their former employer (who threatened legal action) and Microsoft (who made repeated recruitment attempts, including invitations to Redmond headquarters).","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/K8opvOlnnQQ/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-14T23:30:13.000Z"},{"id":"7QBfIzCMs","title":"How IntelliJ IDEA was built around developer flow","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vz7_ZJbbZhI","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-secret-to-seamless-development-flow-with-intellij-idea-7qbfizcms","summary":"IntelliJ IDEA's development philosophy centers on maintaining developer 'flow' \u2014 a state of focused, uninterrupted productivity. Speed and rapid feedback loops are highlighted as critical to a satisfying development experience. The IDE's core abstraction, PSI (Program Structure Interface or Program Source Interface), has been foundational since the beginning and remains central to how IntelliJ represents source code, its syntactic elements, and their connections, even in 2025.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Vz7_ZJbbZhI/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-12T23:00:41.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["getinstance","django","volvo","nette","implementing"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","tbpn","alexfinn","hamelhusain","ryolu_"],"similar":[{"id":"getinstance","handle":"getinstance","name":"Getinstance","is_squad":false,"x":-5.3807,"y":1.9524,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":31,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/632907c295a545c3989228073b452b22","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.695971,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":5.903226,"tag_diversity":0.709677},"top_tags_preview":[["php",22],["general-programming",13],["python",13]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-1.4706,-2.9559],"cadence_depth":[-6.6176,0.1324],"hype_variety":[-7.7941,-7.7794],"title_style":[7.0441,-6.4706]}},{"id":"django","handle":"django","name":"Django","is_squad":false,"x":-4.8973,"y":1.9228,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":252,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/4a658d547a52423e99fe641ecc576195","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.86353,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.02381,"avg_read_time":2.68018,"tag_diversity":0.186508},"top_tags_preview":[["django",223],["python",120],["open-source",71]],"view_coords":{"engage